Entry value hole
description: the value_hole state
- >
  The entry's marker is drawn (`- `, or the key with its colon) and the empty value cell after it
  holds the cursor. `dash_space` / `key_colon_space` here open the nested structure COMPACTLY -
  the fresh marker and its value cell stay on THIS row
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`alphanumeric`', '', '[unquoted_scalar_appending](*::server:yamlover-editor:unquoted_scalar_appending)']
  - ['`asterisk`', '', '[pointer_entry](*::server:yamlover-editor:pointer_entry)']
  - ['`pipe`', '', '[block_scalar_editing](*::server:yamlover-editor:block_scalar_editing)']
  - ['`open_brace`', '', '[flow_map_editing](*::server:yamlover-editor:flow_map_editing)']
  - ['`open_bracket`', '', '[flow_seq_editing](*::server:yamlover-editor:flow_seq_editing)']
  - ['`dash_space`', '', '`value_hole` (stays)']
  - ['`key_colon_space`', 'the key already exists in the node', '[error_flash](*::server:yamlover-editor:error_flash)']
  - ['`key_colon_space`', 'otherwise', '`value_hole` (stays)']
  - ['`key_colon_enter`', '', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`enter`', '', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'an uncommitted key - the colon is undone, its text (quoted spelling kept) returns to the hole', '[unquoted_scalar_appending](*::server:yamlover-editor:unquoted_scalar_appending)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'an uncommitted dash - the marker is undone', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise', '[focus_prev](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_prev)']
  - ['`tab`', 'a previous ordinal sibling exists', '`value_hole` (stays)']
  - ['`tab`', 'otherwise', '[nop](*::server:yamlover-editor:nop)']
  - ['`shift_tab`', 'the entry is below the root level', '`value_hole` (stays)']
  - ['`shift_tab`', 'otherwise', '[nop](*::server:yamlover-editor:nop)']
  - ['`up_arrow`', '', '[focus_prev](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_prev)']
  - ['`down_arrow`', '', '[focus_next](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_next)']
